  "notes": "This portable C++ scenario uses only the official IEEE 1516.1 C++ API and standard library. It checks subscriber-local forgetting and handle-to-name lookup, then verifies orphan deletion through two transitions: the owner unpublishes and divests all attributes before locally forgetting the last-known instance, and a publisher resigns with UNCONDITIONALLY_DIVEST_ATTRIBUTES after the subscriber has locally forgotten a second instance. In both cases, a surviving federate successfully reserves the prior object name.",
